    "verifier_justification": "The diff removes five module-local derived rules in a chapter 61 (knitted apparel) composition whose formulas were equalities against statistical reporting numbers from other chapters (7202.11.10.00 ferroalloy, 7601.10.30.00 aluminum wire, 9506.62.40.40 footballs, 2203.00.00.30 beer, 8541.42.00.10 PV cells), each carrying proof atoms citing those foreign-chapter provisions, and makes the identifiers caller inputs. Those flags were the gates for this module's §301 list 1/4A component, §232 aluminum, §201 solar, §338 alcohol, §122 surcharge and the 9903.01.32 reciprocal-annex exclusion (e.g. entry_is_reciprocal_annex_excluded's formula is just entry_is_line_a), so every one of those cited action provisions was grounded on a line no chapter 61 entry can match — a condition with no basis in the cited source, which the fix removes and re-grounds on membership classification. The PR body treats the old coupling as producing wrong law (\"unlawfully suppressed the surcharge on §301-member lines for all origins\"), so this is a fidelity correction and not a pure refactor, and the change is far more than metadata, so it is not mechanical. I could not refute either the classification or the kind; untraceable_branch fits better than wrong_entity_or_scope because the decisive act is the removal of foreign-provision-grounded conditions, not a re-targeting of the entity or population.",
    "verifier_quote": "-  - formula: (((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((hts_number == \"9506.62.40.40\")))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))",
    "verifier_notes": "inferred from verified sibling module index 60 (same kind and rule path in this chunk). Verified against both file versions (pre 956a547418, post 2a6bdb01de). Two caveats for a reviewer: (1) the repair is partial at this commit — `entry_is_energy_resource` in the post file (line 1950) still reads `hts_number == \"7202.11.10.00\"`, the same exemplar-grounding pattern, so the commit targeted only the five named `entry_is_line_*` slots; (2) `section_122_component_rate` (post line 2526) still carries `if entry_is_line_a or entry_is_line_b: 0 else: temporary_import_surcharge_rate` at this commit — the membership re-gating described in the PR body (entry_is_section_122_exempt / entry_is_section_232_covered) lands in other commits of stacked PR #1300, so this file's consumers are byte-unchanged here and only the flag definitions moved. Also note the retained boilerplate in the rewritten summary (\"This deterministic RuleSpec serialization changes no formula tokens, dates, inputs, proof atoms, or runtime values ... runtime semantics are unchanged\") is stale/false for this change: the five identifiers move from module-local derived rules to caller inputs, so chapter 61 outputs that were dead-false can now fire. The commit body is a bare subject line (\"b1.6: make generated entry flags caller inputs\") with no further message; evidence of intent comes from the PR body and the maintainer issue comment (\"c and e are fully replaced and no longer valid input slots\"). No corpus provision lookup was needed: the kind turns on chapter-scoping of HTS numbers, which the diff settles.",
